link::no-memory-map

  × the program has no `memory` block
  help: a program built into an executable declares exactly one, giving the board's memory and
        what each region holds (ADR 0057), such as:
        memory {
            region FLASH { origin: 0x0800_0000, size: 0x1_0000 }
            region RAM { origin: 0x2000_0000, size: 0x4000 }
            code in FLASH;
            data in RAM;
            stack in RAM { size: 0x800 }
        }
